 to say I did  nothing wrong if the partisan Dems ever  tried to impeach I would first head to  the US Supreme Court the analysis here  is really simple impeachment and removal  of the president works like this the  House of Representatives files articles  of impeachment and sort of works as the  prosecutor the Senate then votes almost  like they are the jury and ultimately  decides whether or not to remove the  president from power there's nothing in  there that includes the possibility of  going to the Supreme Court period the  power of the House and Senate to bring  and investigate and adjudicate  impeachment is their sole power the  house brings charges the Senate is like  the jury period there's no mechanism to  appeal to the Supreme Court the Supreme  Court decides whether or not to hear  previously decided cases which have  requested appeal impeachment is a  congressional process this isn't an  argument I'm making for or against  impeachment it's just another one of  these examples of Trump doesn't get it  and it's really important to understand  this  Trump claiming that he will try to use  the Supreme Court to block impeachment  fits two common themes of the Trump  presidency  theme number one Trump doesn't actually  understand how the Constitution or  checks and balances or government work  okay that's theme number one which is  fomented confirmed by Trump saying he  would try to use the Supreme Court to  block impeachment number two it's  Trump's autocratic authoritarian  tendencies thinking that the Supreme  Court has anything to do with  impeachment and that Trump could go to  the Supreme Court and say hey stop the  impeachment from happening that shows  like with much other material that we  have that Trump has a fundamental lack  of understanding of how any of this  stuff works confirmed once again but of  course the idea that Trump could go to  the Supreme Court which is now made up  one-third of by people made made up to  33 percent of people who Tr